# Local dev SQLite database -- was accidentally committed (with real, if
# test, user data in it) in the "wiki updates" commit; untracked and added
# here 2026-08-29 once found. Keep out of git going forward -- local dev
# state, not something to ship in the repo.
backend/_dev_site.db

# graphify (knowledge-graph tool output) -- local analysis artifacts, not
# meant to ship in the repo (extraction sidecars, cache/, cost tracking,
# raw graph.json, graph.html). graph.html was tracked for a while so it
# could be shared/reviewed without regenerating it, but it's a large
# (~1MB) generated file that changes on every graphify rebuild -- pure
# git churn with no diffable content -- so it's untracked again as of
# 2026-08-31, per explicit user decision. Regenerate locally
# (`graphify export html` or a full `/graphify` run) whenever needed.
#
# Deliberately unanchored (no leading slash, no trailing /*) -- the
# previous `graphify-out/*` had a slash in the middle, which git anchors
# to the directory the .gitignore lives in (repo root), so it only ever
# matched a top-level graphify-out/ and silently missed a nested one
# (found live: frontend/graphify-out/ sat untracked and unignored).
# Same bug shape as the lib/ incident above, inverted -- that one was too
# broad, this one was too narrow. Matching at any depth, like
# __pycache__/ and .pytest_cache/ already do above, is what's wanted here.
graphify-out/

# OS junk files -- previously only ignored inside frontend/.gitignore
# (.DS_Store), which doesn't cover backend/, docs/, or the repo root.
# Added here so Mac/Windows collaborators don't need a personal global
# gitignore just to keep these out of a PR diff.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Claude Code's own per-user local settings/permissions -- .claude/settings.json
# (shared, team-wide config) stays tracked; this file holds one person's
# local overrides and shouldn't be committed. Doesn't exist in this repo
# yet as of this line being added -- added proactively so it's covered
# the moment it does, rather than after an accidental commit.
.claude/settings.local.json

# skills-lock.json (npx-skills / skills.sh package manager) -- a lockfile
# for globally-installed Claude Code skills, written to whatever directory
# `npx skills add ... --global` happened to run from. It doesn't describe
# anything about this project (the skills it locks went to ~/.claude/skills/,
# not here) -- an artifact of where a command was run, not a real dependency
# of this repo.
skills-lock.json
